WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.830
This AI agent's trade goes through.

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.140
Its owner switches it off.

3
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.320
The same trade is refused, on chain.

4
00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:14.517
This is trustset, the trust stack for AI
agents on Monad.

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.528
In the last year, AI agents and trading
bots lost about ten million dollars,

6
00:00:21.568 --> 00:00:24.120
across thirteen public incidents.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:27.294
When TradeWiz stopped its bot,

8
00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:31.457
seventy-three percent of the drain
happened after the stop.

9
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.700
The stop lived inside one app.

10
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.790
The key worked everywhere else.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:41.963
trustset moves the stop on chain.

12
00:00:42.003 --> 00:00:45.136
An agent's status lives in one contract,

13
00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:49.023
and every app that checks asks it before
it acts.

14
00:00:49.063 --> 00:00:52.913
Off means refused, everywhere at once.

15
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.010
The off switch is the first layer.

16
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.800
A stop can be made final.

17
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.010
A passkey can pause an agent with no
wallet and no gas.

18
00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.080
Guardians can vote to pause it.

19
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.580
It can expire on a date you set.

20
00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.040
And if a paid agent doesn't deliver, the
payer gets the money back.

21
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.180
Every one of these is a real transaction
on Monad testnet.

22
00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:21.927
Eight layers, each its own contract.

23
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:23.907
Why Monad?

24
00:01:23.947 --> 00:01:28.017
Every app that checks honours a stop from
the very next block.

25
00:01:28.057 --> 00:01:33.034
And passkeys are verified on chain by
Monad's P256 precompile,

26
00:01:33.074 --> 00:01:35.947
so the panic button needs no wallet.

27
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.723
It's live today.

28
00:01:38.763 --> 00:01:42.573
Thirty-one agents registered, more than a
thousand events on chain.

29
00:01:42.613 --> 00:01:45.791
The contracts are immutable, with no admin
key,

30
00:01:45.831 --> 00:01:50.583
and every build runs a hundred and
twenty-eight thousand fuzzed calls.

31
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:57.087
Every agent that holds a key needs a stop
that works outside its own app.

32
00:01:58.183 --> 00:01:59.813
We're Silk Nodes.

33
00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:04.594
We've run validators since 2021, across
more than twenty networks,

34
00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.853
Monad included, with zero slashing
incidents.

35
00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:11.693
Running keys taught us they need an off
switch.

36
00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:18.123
Next, we're taking trustset to Monad's
DEXs and protocols.

37
00:02:18.163 --> 00:02:23.133
One check in their contracts, and every
agent on Monad has a stop.

38
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:28.007
trustset.silknodes.io

